  "theorem_name": "IntervalKKTGapStabilityAndVanishingEntrywiseRadiusNoGo",
  "declared_proposition": "Let K_tilde be real symmetric with gamma=min_j |lambda_j(K_tilde)|>0. Every symmetric K=K_tilde+E with ||E||_2<gamma has the same inertia; the computable interval condition sqrt(sum_ij r_ij^2)<gamma is sufficient. Vanishing maximum entry radius alone is not a dimension-uniform substitute: for diag(I_n,-I_r), the positive-block perturbation -(2/n)J_n has entry radius 2/n tending to zero but changes one eigenvalue from 1 to -1.",
  "mathematical_argument": "Weyl's inequality moves every ordered eigenvalue by at most ||E||_2, so no eigenvalue can cross zero when ||E||_2<gamma. The interval Frobenius radius dominates the operator norm. For the no-go, J_n has eigenvalues n,0,...,0; therefore I_n-(2/n)J_n has eigenvalues -1,1,...,1 although every perturbation entry is 2/n. The stable comparison I_n-(1/(2n))J_n has eigenvalues 1/2,1,...,1 and satisfies the gap condition exactly.",
